    fix(frontend): close the raw-enum leak on every path, and scan the screen instead of one node (ORD-0222)
    
    ORD-0208 ④ fixed one of four print points.  The day card has two render paths, and the
    other one still printed the provider mode and interpolated the anchor enum into the
    「{type}锚点」 template; the live ETA row, both route-evidence rows and the studio walking
    figure did the same with their own values, and the route durations were hardcoded English
    inside a Chinese screen.
    
    - day-card row, ETA row and both route rows now go through modeLabel/anchorLabel, and the
      anchor's template receives an already translated word
    - live.routeDuration / live.slack / studio.walkingMinutes move the minute wording into i18n
    - the day heading renders the weekday from the payload's own ISO date instead of the
      server's English label; activity titles stay server content and are handed off, not
      mapped, per the arbitration
    - unknown mode/anchor fail closed in Chinese (未识别的出行方式 / 未识别) instead of
      humanising a token into the screen
    - new gate scans the whole rendered screen in two layers (visual, accessible) across
      hub/live/map/studio, in light and dark, and refuses a vacuous pass by requiring every
      touched row to have been seen; killAA1 puts the raw enum back and turns it red

